From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:40:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 116/136] test(refinery): characterize every merge-push lane
 end to end (gcp-l8td.4)

B1 phase 3, step 1. Before B1.2a (gcp-l8td.5) moves the refinery's merge
lane out of mol-refinery-patrol into a script, pin what the lane does
today, so the move can be proven to run the same way. Before this, the mr
lane, the post-merge close and both cleanups had no executed test, and the
mr lane is dormant (every rig lands direct), so moving that code could
break it silently.

The formula change is comment lines only. 16 `# --- merge-lane:<name>:
begin/end ---` pairs wrap the merge-push blocks that no earlier suite
sentinelled: read-metadata, strategy, block-existing-pr, github-helpers,
direct-close/-cleanup, the eleven mr blocks, and local. The blocks the
other suites already pin (origin-repo-resolution, the approval-gate
wiring, merge-state-helpers/-gate and merge-ff-push) keep their sentinels
unchanged.

gastown/tests/test_refinery_merge_lanes.sh runs 23 cases against real git:
a bare origin, a polecat clone, and a refinery clone with `temp` rebased.
Each case asserts the bead the lane leaves behind (metadata, status, close
reason), the gc/gh/curl calls it made, and the refs it moved. Every block
is extracted by sentinel and rendered from [vars], then stitched in lane
order. The branching glue cites the prose line it transcribes, and the
lane is chosen by running the shared prefix, so the approval and
existing_pr promotions to mr are real. The direct lane runs as two
processes because the merge-state gate exits the shell. The one
transcribed command is the prose-only branch delete (:1947), and the
extractor fails if that line moves. Lanes run under `env -i` with a PATH
of symlinked tools plus gc/gh/curl stubs and a git shim for `remote
get-url origin`. So "gh absent" is real, no agent GC_* variable leaks in,
and any unmodelled call fails the case. 4b runs the real
merge-approval-gate.sh.

Two places where today's behaviour differs from the brief, pinned as-is:
- With existing_pr set, the lane reads that PR twice, not once.
  github-helpers validates it (:1420-1472) before any lane runs, and
  mr-verify reads it again.
- For the same reason, the six existing_pr refusals fire from that
  validation. Its messages are identical to mr-verify's twins.
The mr cleanup case asserts TODAY's failure: `git checkout "$TARGET"`
refuses while the target is checked out in another worktree, and `temp`
survives. gcp-l8td.6 (B1.2b) is the fix, and it flips that case.

Validation: the suite passes (23 cases). It fails with the missing block
named when one begin sentinel is deleted from a scratch copy, and it fails
against origin/integration a5e1e2fb's formula (all 16 blocks missing). A
mutant formula (close reason, 4a merge_result, mr cleanup checkout)
turns exactly the owning cases red.

